  "titles": {
    "power": "05 | Regulated camera, radio and GPS port supplies",
    "telemetry": "15 | External GPS and radio UART ports"
  },
  "notes": {
    "power": [
      "R10 O5: RAW_PROTECTED -> AP63201 5.456V -> camera limiter; TPS7A91 4.792V -> separate GPS and radio limiters.",
      "All three TPS2553 enables have 100k pull-downs; fault pull-ups use main 3V3 only. R405 sets the LDO minimum load.",
      "Switch current limits and endpoint-voltage budgets: sources/r10_design/parts_qualification.md. Bench transient/inrush verification remains required.",
      "Firmware: disable UART OE before port power; hold all EN/OE low throughout reset, boot and load shedding. FAULT delay is not battery-drop detection."
    ],
    "telemetry": [
      "R10: external GPS J410 and radio J420. GH4 pins 1 supply, 2 GND, 3 board TX, 4 board RX; harness crosses TX to endpoint RX.",
      "GPS USART6 PC6 TX / PC7 RX AF7; radio UART5 PB13 TX / PB12 RX AF14 (DS12110 Rev10 Table11 p90).",
      "TXU0202 VCCA = main 3V3, VCCB = own switched TPS70933 output. OE has 10k pull-down. 1k UART series resistors and ground-only ESD clamps.",
      "Reset / boot / off: EN=0 and OE=0. Startup: EN, stable downstream supply, UART idle-high configuration, then OE. Shutdown: OE low before EN low.",
      "Radio USB-powered with board off: TXU partial-power-down isolation protects MCU; power-pin reverse/transient qualification remains a separate bench gate.",
      "Radio messages may never arm/fire; no port signal reaches pyro, arming or actuator nets. Configure LR900 channels within 902-928MHz."
    ],
    "servos": [
      "R10 O3/O6: J122 signal pins1/4/7/10; pins3/6/9/12 board GND for signal reference only; pins2/5/8/11 have NO BOARD CONNECTION.",
      "Each servo power AND return run directly to the pack in the harness. Parallel residual board-return current must satisfy the documented harness calculation.",
      "The board cannot disconnect servo power. Servo neutral/failsafe during reset is a harness and servo qualification requirement.",
      "Retained: four 1k series resistors, 10k MCU-side pull-downs and SRV05-4 clamp."
    ],
    "actuator_power": [
      "R10: Q120/Q121 and gate network retained as the pyro-bus load switch; RAW_ACT feeds J124 and RAW_ACT sensing only.",
      "C121 removed; servos use external pack power and return. The ARM plug remains a complete break; no feed directly from BAT_IN or RAW_PROTECTED.",
      "R134 limits a shorted igniter; firmware ends each fire pulse within20ms. Copper and harness pulse qualification remains required."
    ],
    "pyro": [
      "R10: one recovery channel, unchanged functional fire/gate/sense network. J124.2 RAW_ACT, J124.1 BUS; J121.2 IGN, J121.1 OUT.",
      "ARM plug is the complete electrical break: fit last, remove first. Black3.5mm terminals enter from -x; direct J124 pad/copper gap >=1.5mm.",
      "R10 uses default board clearance; accepted loss of R9 single-defect spacing margins does not waive functional reset, gate or divider safety.",
      "Ground ARM/continuity checks refuse firing; in flight readings only log/annunciate and never veto a fire. Firmware fire timeout <=20ms."
